  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Abydos Solar II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Project promises strong development impact in Egypt as it will (i) expand solar capacity which will lower the average cost of electricity generation by displacing inefficient and more expensive power generation sources; (ii) contribute to GHG emissions avoidance; (iii) enhance the power sectors resilience by diversifying the countrys power generation mix; (iv) by incorporating BESS, it can support shifting generation from lower demand daytime hours to dispatch during peak consumption hours at night; and (v) support knowledge transfers to facilitate future renewable energy investments with BESS.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project consists of the development, financing, construction, operation and maintenance of a 1,000MWac solar Photovoltaic (PV) Power plant with 600MWh Battery Energy Storage System (BESS), located in Aswan Governorate, Egypt, under the terms of a 25-year Power Purchase Agreement with the Egypt Electricity Transmission Company, fully guaranteed by Egypt&apos;s Ministry of Finance.</narrative>
  </description>
